WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.500
The SCP Foundation specializes in tracking
anomalous creatures, entities or objects,

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.270
and protecting mankind by keeping these anomalies
contained.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.330
It doesn’t happen very often though, that
an SCP surrenders itself to the Foundation,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.290
offering to be contained without putting up
a fight.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.200
You might think that would be a welcome change
for the Foundation’s personnel, getting

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.130
an easy containment like that rather than
having to devote valuable time, resources,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.120
and even lives to capturing an anomaly.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.059
But then you have to ask the obvious and worrying
questions.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:38.199
How did this anomaly know where to find the
Foundation so that it could turn itself in

00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:39.890
in the first place?

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.790
Did somebody send it, and if so, why?

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:48.129
Well don’t worry, you don’t need to try
and imagine this scenario, because an SCP

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:53.480
turning itself over to the Foundation under
mysterious circumstances has actually already

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.480
happened.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.229
One day, security personnel at an SCP Foundation
containment site opened the front door to

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:02.329
find an SCP just sitting there on the doorstep.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:07.890
The anomaly was brought in for questioning,
and while it was soon designated SCP-032,

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:12.590
it has sometimes been known by another name:
Brother’s Bride.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:17.619
SCP-032 is a person, or rather a replica of
a person.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:21.920
Not a living statue that moves whenever you
look away, or a waxwork that comes to life

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.580
when the sun goes down.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.500
No, this replica is far stranger.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.700
SCP-032 resembles a human woman around thirty
years of age.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:36.780
Who made her, who she is supposed to resemble,
and just where exactly she came from are all

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.759
still questions the Foundation have been unable
to answer.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:45.070
But what their research teams have been able
to determine is what she is made from.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:50.220
Brother’s Bride consists largely of plastics,
at least the external portion of her body.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:55.350
Her “skin” is made from a combination
of 5.5 millimeter thick silicone and other

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.210
plastic fiber polymers, all colored with a
pigment to more closely mimic the shade of

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.540
Caucasian human skin.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:08.110
SCP-032 has been referred to as a “Type-F
human simulacrum” by the Foundation, meaning

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:13.320
that she has an imperfect outward resemblance
to a human being, and the internal workings

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.030
of her body are drastically different from
an ordinary human’s organs or central nervous

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.030
system.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.330
What does SCP-032 have instead?

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:26.350
Well, she lacks a skeleton or any of the other
internal parts that make up a human body.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.220
Instead, her insides are entirely refined
liquid oil.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:35.570
However, in spite of having no bones, no organs,
and existing as just pure oil filling up a

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:42.450
plastic skin, SCP-032 has no problem moving
on her own, or communicating verbally.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:47.080
When she was first discovered waiting outside
the Foundation’s Slovakian compound, Brother’s

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.370
Bride claimed she had come there “to be
stored.”

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:56.190
SCP-032 is imperfect in how closely she resembles
a human being, and this becomes more apparent

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.770
the closer one gets to her.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:02.600
At a distance, she can maintain some illusion
of appearing to be fully human.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.610
However, her appearance becomes less and less
convincing as someone approaches.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:11.690
Naturally, the sight of an uncanny, rubbery
almost-human is enough to unsettle someone,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.910
perhaps even cause discomfort.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:19.700
But this also happens to be unrelated to SCP-032’s
anomalous abilities, which she detailed to

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.970
Foundation personnel when she was first contained.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:28.090
The Foundation security team that discovered
SCP-032, patiently sitting and waiting to

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.980
be found, questioned her motives and how she
had come to be there.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.760
There was no record of what time she might
have arrived on the compound’s security

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.480
cameras, and SCP-032 gave the personnel no
inkling as to how she knew the location of

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.090
the Foundation’s Slovakian site.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:49.060
Somehow, she’d managed to approach without
being spotted by anyone, but would not explain

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.180
how she had done so.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.100
Security personnel at the site were obviously
skeptical, and asked Brother’s Bride why

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.300
she had come to the Foundation.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:03.330
SCP-032 claimed that her creators had commanded
her to, that she was to be placed in “indefinite

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.650
storage, until claimed”.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.980
Although the silicone-based woman appears
to possess a normal level of cognitive function,

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:15.510
she claims she is not fully sapient, meaning
SCP-032 does not possess the intelligence

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:20.440
or understanding of other human beings, at
least according to her.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:27.311
By her own admission, SCP-032 is an intermediary,
acting on behalf of her creators, although

00:04:27.311 --> 00:04:31.090
the SCP Foundation has yet to be able to verify
this.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.340
As for her anomalous abilities, SCP-032 was
kind enough to detail these to the security

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.320
personnel that first found her.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.280
She has an innate ability to influence any
biological entity in her immediate vicinity.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.060
In other words, any organism that gets too
close.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.440
Well, not quite any, there is a limitation
to her power.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.820
SCP-032 can only affect a creature or organism
not created by, related to, or influenced

00:04:58.820 --> 00:04:59.820
by humanity.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:06.090
So, plants, animals, even microorganisms like
bacteria, all fall into the category of things

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:09.750
that SCP-032 has an effect on.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.970
According to the various tests the Foundation’s
researchers have conducted, the exact nature

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:17.910
of how SCP-032’s abilities work seems to
vary.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.910
But her presence always causes massive and
irreversible damage to an animal or organism’s

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.370
ability to exchange or use energy.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:30.910
For example, when SCP-032 is surrounded by
wild flora, these plants will lose the ability

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.880
to conduct the process of photosynthesis.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.990
They therefore can no longer produce or consume
energy, preventing them from continued growth

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.470
and ultimately causing death.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:47.010
In much the same vein, any animals that come
into close contact with SCP-032 will find

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:52.160
themselves unable to use their respiratory
or digestive systems, rendering them unable

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.740
to breathe oxygen, or properly consume food.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:01.360
Not even germs and other microorganisms are
safe from SCP-032’s effects, although when

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:06.190
it comes to these microscopic life forms,
her ability seems to focus solely on their

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:11.550
reproductive systems, and if bacteria cannot
divide itself, it cannot spread.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:17.650
At present, the SCP Foundation keeps Brother’s
Bride housed in an automated containment unit,

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:21.230
restricting the amount of direct contact personnel
can have with her.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:25.889
Unless they are there to conduct authorized
experiments, or other necessary research related

00:06:25.889 --> 00:06:30.760
tasks, staff are to leave SCP-032 alone.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.870
Any interviews with her are not even carried
out in person, and instead researchers use

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:41.460
a remote communication array to ask SCP-032
more about her origin, her creators, and her

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.460
abilities.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.090
This probably seems a little over-cautious,
right?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:50.810
After all, SCP-032 has no effect on the human
body, and isn’t aggressive or outwardly

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:51.810
hostile.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.400
Maybe locking her in a room is excessive.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.490
But remember, her degenerative abilities do
affect microorganisms and bacteria, even those

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.949
that are beneficial to human beings.

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:07.510
The human body is full of good bacteria that
aids with digestion and helps the body absorb

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:12.240
nutrients - like the ones you’ve heard about
in ads for probiotic yogurt.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.290
Since 032’s effects don’t discriminate
between “good” and “bad” bacteria,

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:22.580
people have to keep their distance from SCP-032
or else they might find that they can no longer

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.160
digest food properly.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:31.120
In fact, no biological material is allowed
anywhere near her, no house plants, no pets,

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.120
nothing.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:38.010
Oddly, SCP-032 herself seems fine with this,
and has never expressed any desire for any

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:43.210
form of comfort, and does not appear to require
sustenance like food or water.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:48.900
Shortly after she was first contained by the
SCP Foundation, SCP-032 was interviewed by

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:54.710
Doctor Alexander Kovac, the resident psychologist
at the site where Brother’s Bride was discovered.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:08:00.990
Doctor Kovac initially tried to ask SCP-032
to disclose her name, however she was unable

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:01.990
to do so.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:03.540
“I don't have one.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.580
People have names.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.070
I'm not one.”

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:10.460
She then went on to explain that even her
creators had no name for her, and that she

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:14.040
was instructed to cooperate with the SCP Foundation.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.510
Doctor Kovac pressed on, asking about when
she’d told security that she was to be stored

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:22.931
until collected, who SCP-032 had meant was
coming to collect her.

00:08:22.931 --> 00:08:28.390
Her answer was as enigmatic as could be expected,
she claimed that she was going to be collected

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:33.959
by someone her creators wished to torment,
and finding her in the hands of the SCP Foundation

00:08:33.959 --> 00:08:36.699
would bring this person greater suffering.

00:08:36.699 --> 00:08:42.169
Kovac asked if this person was a part of the
Foundation, assuming that SCP-032’s creators

00:08:42.169 --> 00:08:47.499
had some kind of animosity towards a particular
member of personnel and that 032 was part

00:08:47.499 --> 00:08:51.750
of some kind of revenge plot against a member
of Foundation staff.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:56.149
SCP-032 denied this though, stating “He
is not one of you.

00:08:56.149 --> 00:08:58.730
Merely a one-time sympathizer, of sorts.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:03.759
He believes you tried to help him once, and
if he is forced here, if he finds me here,

00:09:03.759 --> 00:09:04.930
you will die.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:05.930
That will hurt him.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.200
They have no interest in any of you, or your
organization.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.510
You are here as a tool, just as I am.”

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:18.319
According to SCP-032, the man coming to collect
her was a prideful, complacent figure, who

00:09:18.319 --> 00:09:20.120
“won when he should have lost”.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:24.160
Somehow, this individual had apparently been
punished by being forced to live in exile

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:31.300
from his kin and wander the world endlessly,
destroying anything in his path, yet unwillingly.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:37.080
His very presence would poison human beings,
leaving this man trapped in eternal solitude,

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.779
tormented by the weight of his guilty conscience.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:44.529
SCP-032 described the man’s punishment as
a “masterwork of torment”.

00:09:44.529 --> 00:09:49.389
She described her purpose in being sent to
the Foundation as being to act as this man’s

00:09:49.389 --> 00:09:51.050
last undoing.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:55.931
Apparently, this wanderer would occasionally
find solace in looking at nature, and find

00:09:55.931 --> 00:09:58.000
hope in the world around him.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:03.360
Her ability to destroy the organisms around
her would be a way to break this man’s will,

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.639
the final nail in the proverbial coffin.

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:11.459
Apparently, SCP-032’s appearance was also
seemingly meant to deceive him.

00:10:11.459 --> 00:10:16.170
She stated that the man would recognize her
and this would remind him of fond memories,

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:23.029
but then as he got closer he would see SCP-032
for what she really was, a crude replica of

00:10:23.029 --> 00:10:29.660
a human being, reminding this man that her
likeness would be forever out of his reach.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:35.509
SCP-032 was intended, by her creators, to
be as artificial as the wandering man’s

00:10:35.509 --> 00:10:41.569
hope, and when he eventually found her, either
in a day, a month, or in a century, she would

00:10:41.569 --> 00:10:44.740
destroy his very last source of solace.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:49.540
At the conclusion of the interview, Doctor
Kovac asked why this man would recognize her,

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:54.199
and SCP-032 simply replied “I used to be
his wife.”

00:10:54.199 --> 00:10:59.490
If we take SCP-032 at her word, then it appears
she was created with the intention of being

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:04.610
used to torment this wandering man and act
as a final punishment for him.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:10.170
In another interview six months after her
initial containment, SCP-032 expressed a hatred

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:13.410
for the man’s wife whom she was made to
resemble.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:20.249
Sent in to assess SCP-032’s cognitive abilities,
and personality - or lack of - Doctor Kovac

00:11:20.249 --> 00:11:21.949
questioned this.

00:11:21.949 --> 00:11:27.850
SCP-032 had always been adamant that she had
no conscious thoughts or feelings of her own,

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:32.050
and when challenged by the doctor, she claimed
that she hated her “mold” because her

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.110
creators wanted her to.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:39.429
The first thing SCP-032’s creators had done
after making her was show her the wife of

00:11:39.429 --> 00:11:41.670
the man they hoped to torment.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:48.759
It is unclear whether SCP-032 was shown photographs
or the actual woman she had been molded from.

00:11:48.759 --> 00:11:54.209
Not an easy task as this woman, the wife,
was apparently long dead.

00:11:54.209 --> 00:11:59.899
But the creators had risked disturbing the
wife’s final rest, just to show her to SCP-032.

00:11:59.899 --> 00:12:02.350
“She was beautiful.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:04.339
So peaceful, serene.

00:12:04.339 --> 00:12:05.339
Whole.

00:12:05.339 --> 00:12:11.380
Even gone, even dead, I could see the essence
of who she used to be… of who she still

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.540
was, and forever will be.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.540
Her soul.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:20.519
They told me she didn't get to live for all
that long, but when she lived… she was herself.

00:12:20.519 --> 00:12:21.929
She was alive.

00:12:21.929 --> 00:12:23.639
And so I hated her.”

00:12:23.639 --> 00:12:29.519
In the wife’s face, SCP-032 saw a reflection
of herself, and realized that she had been

00:12:29.519 --> 00:12:35.129
made just to be a mockery, a parody of a living
human being, existing only to cause misery

00:12:35.129 --> 00:12:38.589
to the wandering man who would one day find
her.

00:12:38.589 --> 00:12:44.220
Instead of skin, she had molded silicone and
plastic, synthetic fiber in place of hair

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.009
and oil for blood.

00:12:46.009 --> 00:12:51.170
But what SCP-032 lacked, she realized, was
a soul.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:55.699
This was all part of the Brothers’ design,
according to SCP-032.

00:12:55.699 --> 00:13:00.259
When the man found her, he would see not only
what had been done to the memory of his wife.

00:13:00.259 --> 00:13:07.399
But he’d also see how much SCP-032 hated
her, and hated herself for not being alive

00:13:07.399 --> 00:13:09.579
the same way the wife had been.

00:13:09.579 --> 00:13:11.230
The goal of all this?

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:15.399
To make the man realize that he never won.

00:13:15.399 --> 00:13:22.249
SCP-032 herself is a mystery, but perhaps
the real question is: Who do you think this

00:13:22.249 --> 00:13:25.989
man is, and what was it he didn’t win?

00:13:25.989 --> 00:13:27.989
But that’s a story for another day.

00:13:27.989 --> 00:13:30.139
Let us know what you think down in the comments…

00:13:30.139 --> 00:13:36.920
Now go check out “SCP-5545 - Mysterious
Tunnels in Antarctica - ABNORMALITY” and

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.809
“SCP-1730 - What Happened to Site-13?

00:13:39.809 --> 00:13:44.909
The Full Story Compilation” for more of
the most mysterious SCPs!

